{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5fdb790c826de64","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard-accessibility defects identified by the\n34\taccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows — project creation,\n35\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — so that each\n36\tflow is fully operable by keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable\n37\tcontrols, and consistent visible focus indicators. It delivers the code fixes\n38\tin the Dashboard console that make the renewed conformance statement possible.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Remediate every keyboard-operability defect enumerated in the audit report\n43\t  for the four audited flows:\n44\t  - Eliminate focus loss and focus traps in modals and multi-step dialogs\n45\t    (focus must move into the modal on open, stay trapped while open, return\n46\t    to the invoking control on close).\n47\t  - Make every control in the four flows reachable and operable via keyboard\n48\t    (tab/shift-tab navigation, Enter/Space activation, arrow-key list\n49\t    traversal where the pattern requires it).\n50\t- Apply a consistent, visible focus-indicator style across all controls in the\n51\t  four audited flows, following the console UI kit's focus styling conventions\n52\t  rather than per-flow ad-hoc styles.\n53\t- Add automated keyboard-operability test coverage for the fixed defects in\n54\t  the four flows (keyboard walkthrough tests per flow), so regressions are\n55\t  caught by CI.\n56\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes\n57\t  require, and flows outside the four audited ones.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Given the project creation flow, When a user completes it end-to-end using\n62\t  keyboard only, Then every step succeeds with no focus traps and no\n63\t  unreachable controls.\n64\t- Given the workbench spawn flow, When completed end-to-end using keyboard\n65\t  only, Then every step succeeds with no focus traps and no unreachable\n66\t  controls.\n67\t- Given the model deployment flow, When completed end-to-end using keyboard\n68\t  only, Then every step succeeds with no focus traps and no unreachable\n69\t  controls.\n70\t- Given the pipeline run submission flow, When completed end-to-end using\n71\t  keyboard only, Then every step succeeds with no focus traps and no\n72\t  unreachable controls.\n73\t- Given the audit report's defect list for the four flows, When each defect is\n74\t  re-checked via a keyboard-only walkthrough, Then every enumerated defect is\n75\t  resolved or explicitly dispositioned.\n76\t- Given any interactive control in the four audited flows, When it receives\n77\t  keyboard focus, Then a visible focus indicator is rendered using the shared\n78\t  focus styling convention, consistent across all four flows.\n79\t- Given the added keyboard-operability tests, When the full test suite and the\n80\t  console build pipeline run, Then they pass green.\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n85\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the operability\n86\t  remediation and per-flow walkthrough ACs above.\n87\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n88\t  flows — covered by the shared focus-indicator styling scope and its AC.\n89\t  Bundled with HLR-1 by design: both requirements are satisfied by one\n90\t  remediation pass over the same audit defect list and the same UI surfaces.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a46ed90d748f1ae2","agent_id":"af309e1e158376ac5","session_id":"0821e53a-a893-49db-b129-b134dffec720","uuid":"25019297-3388-4733-9a5b-b157dc6613e0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:00:07.139Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5fdb790c826de64","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
